---
title: Introduction
description: NeoWorks is a personal cloud built on ownership, not surveillance. One identity, your data, encrypted so only you can read it.
---

NeoWorks is a personal cloud platform. You get one identity that works across apps and
devices, and your calendar, contacts, photos and files are encrypted on your devices before
they reach our servers.

Everything is source-available and self-hostable. Run it on our infrastructure, or run your
own node.

## How it fits together

- **oauth** signs you in, issues tokens and hosts the account vault, the one place your
  account key is unlocked.
- **api** stores encrypted data and enforces who may read or write it. It only ever holds
  ciphertext.
- **Apps** run the NeoWorks client library in your browser or on your device. Each app
  receives access to exactly the data you choose to give it.

See the [encryption model](/docs/neoworks/encryption) for how keys work and
[sharing](/docs/neoworks/sharing) for how access is granted and revoked.

## Next steps

- Read the [OAuth guide](/docs/neoworks/oauth) for how apps are authorized.
- Learn how [devices](/docs/neoworks/devices) are registered and revoked.
- Prefer to own everything? See [Self-hosting](/docs/neoworks/self-host).
